JOB TITLE: Senior Mechanical Engineer (3 HC, SEA & TW & NA)
ROLE FAMILY: Engineering
COUNTRY: Malaysia
CITY: Kuala Lumpur
REMOTE:
CONTRACT TYPE: full_time
SALARY: USD 2800.0-5000.0 / month
(I) Key Responsibilities:

1. Design technical solutions and evaluate component cost schedules based on client requirements;
2. Complete detailed project designs, including corresponding drawings, BOMs, pneumatic diagrams, and assembly process specifications;
3. Oversee project timelines and quality control to minimise design and development costs;
4. Assist in resolving anomalies identified during assembly and commissioning, and prepare relevant reports and summaries throughout equipment development;
5. Collaborate with supervisors to establish departmental design standards and standardisation protocols;
6. Demonstrate proficiency in analysing FA reports with strong written communication skills;

(II) Qualifications:

1. Minimum 5 years' independent design and development experience; preference given to candidates with expertise in non-standard projects, A-grade projects, dispensing systems, and 3C automation industries;
2. Solid mechanical design foundation, including familiarity with FA component selection, common mechanical material properties, machining processes, and surface treatments;
3. Proficient in SolidWorks, AutoCAD and related software;
4. Knowledgeable in linkage mechanisms and mechanical analysis; skilled in tolerance analysis;
5. Understanding of project engineering processes, capable of deconstructing or redefining efficient workflows to optimise automation layouts;
6. Creative thinking, strong communication skills, proactive attitude, excellent execution and accountability;
7. Willing to work diligently, adaptable to occasional overtime and business travel, with resilience under pressure;
8. Capable of liaising with clients on proposals, possessing clear thinking and strong communication skills.
9. Must have overseas posting experience (fluent in Chinese/English), restricted to foreign nationals from Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, Southeast Asia (Malaysia/Vietnam/India) or other countries.

(III) Number of Vacancies: 3

JOB TITLE: North America Sales Director
ROLE FAMILY: Sales & BD
COUNTRY:
CITY:
REMOTE: Yes
CONTRACT TYPE: full_time
SALARY: USD 10000.0-14000.0 / month
Key Responsibilities:

1. Develop sales strategies, annual targets, and budgets for vision modules in the North American region; monitor performance against targets; and adjust strategies to ensure revenue and market share goals are met;
2. Build the North American sales team and enhance its capabilities and stability;
3. Lead the development of key accounts in North America (across industries such as industrial, consumer electronics, security, and automotive), spearhead negotiations and contract signings for major projects, and maintain high-level partnerships;
4. Collaborate with R&D, Product, and Supply Chain departments to drive the implementation of vision solutions, manage the full lifecycle of major projects, resolve cross-departmental collaboration issues, and ensure delivery;
5. Monitor North American market policies, competitive products, and technology trends; produce analytical reports; lead high-level business events (summits/trade shows) to enhance the brand's premium influence.

Qualifications:

1. 5-10 years of B2B international sales experience, with at least 3 years of sales management experience in the North American region; experience in the camera, vision solutions, AIoT, or smart hardware industries is preferred;
2. Proven experience leading a team to achieve annual revenue in the tens of millions, with a track record of securing large-scale project contracts and maintaining relationships with key clients;
3. Strong capabilities in strategic planning, team leadership, high-level negotiations, cross-departmental collaboration, and risk management;
4. Native-level proficiency in English for business communication, with familiarity with industry terminology;
5. Results-oriented, able to handle performance pressure, and possess strong cross-cultural communication skills.
